    "q-96430": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96430",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int 5{coth}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-1={csch}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{coth}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5({csch}^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (5{csch}^{2}⁡x+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+5x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
